/P 147 0 R
/E (  When you're writing a book, it's not 5000 words a day. It's 300 words that you could do again tomorrow without dread. When you're learning to code, it's 30 minutes, not five hours until your brain melts. When you're building a business, it's the work that moves it forward without crushing you.)
